Inspection points: which street lights are out, which drains to clean

Data in data/ is derived from:
- Lights, poles, stormwater pits, stormwater end structures and stormwater pipes: City of Gold Coast Open Data,
  licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
- Street lamps and roads: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database Licence (ODbL),
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/. Rows with source OSM, the dark stretches and expected_lights.csv
  are derived from OpenStreetMap and stay under the ODbL.

The council-derived data is released under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA), with these credits kept.
The notebook and code are released under the MIT licence (LICENSE).

The night patrol (patrol_trace.csv, patrol_taps.csv), the silt survey in pits.csv and cleaning_priority.csv, and
everything in data/site/ (a made-up site and a simulated emergency lighting test) are simulated to show the
workflow. They are not real inspection data. Costs are indicative, not quotes.

This is independent work using open data, not endorsed by the City of Gold Coast.
